WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.635
In 1840, the Opium War broke out.

00:00:03.635 --> 00:00:07.565
The cause of the war was related to the opium trade.

00:00:07.565 --> 00:00:10.797
When Emperor Daoguang heard the report, he was furious.

00:00:10.797 --> 00:00:13.495
Lin Zexu destroyed a large quantity of opium at Humen.

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:19.170
White smoke rose over the beach, and the people clapped and cheered.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:22.639
It took more than twenty full days for the destruction to be completely finished.

00:00:22.639 --> 00:00:26.795
British warships sailed in from the distant sea.

00:00:26.795 --> 00:00:30.497
The Qing army resisted with all its might, but its weapons were too outdated.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.717
The war lasted two years, and the Qing dynasty was finally defeated.

00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:38.181
In 1842, the two sides signed the Treaty of Nanjing.

00:00:38.181 --> 00:00:41.435
The coastal forts could not withstand the attack either.

00:00:41.435 --> 00:00:44.943
Hong Kong Island was ceded, and trading ports were opened.

00:00:44.943 --> 00:00:47.295
This was an important turning point in modern Chinese history.

00:00:47.295 --> 00:00:51.482
The people who signed felt heavy-hearted and conflicted.

00:00:51.482 --> 00:00:54.257
Many people began to think about ways to save the country.

00:00:54.257 --> 00:00:57.760
The ancient empire faced entirely new challenges.
